// src/lsp/lsp.zen
// The language server, and the folder's surface.
//
// `PLAN.md` stage 4 and `docs/design_lsp.md` are what this folder is
// graded against. `DESIGN.md:45` fixes its shape in one sentence — the
// LSP is "a thin server over compiler internals" — and the way to check
// that claim is to notice that NOTHING IN THIS FOLDER ANSWERS A
// QUESTION ABOUT ZEN. `lsp_hover.zen` calls `expr_node_at` and reads
// `expr_memo`; where a query is missing the fix belongs in `src/sema/`
// or `src/ast/`, never here.
//
// A folder root is a file of starred re-exports and nothing else. A
// name absent from this list is module-private on purpose.
//
//   lsp_pos.zen        the wire's coordinates and this language's
//   lsp_json.zen       JSON as a value, an arena, and the writer
//   lsp_json_read.zen  JSON in
//   lsp_frame.zen      Content-Length framing
//   lsp_decl.zen       which declared name a position is inside
//   lsp_uri.zen        a document URI, as a path the compiler can open
//   lsp_hover.zen      the one query wired to sema
//   lsp_diag.zen       publishDiagnostics: the build, grouped by file
//   lsp_serve.zen      lifecycle, the overlay, and the dispatch table
//   lsp_stdio.zen      the pipe: frames in on stdin, frames out on stdout
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IS BUILT: L1 whole — transport, lifecycle, sync and diagnostics
// — plus ONE query.
//
// `initialize`, `shutdown`, `textDocument/hover`, Full document sync,
// and `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` from all three phases, over
// stdio — `zen lsp` with no arguments is what an editor launches, and
// `std.env.Stdin` is the capability that made it possible. Everything
// else in `design_lsp.md` §2's table is refused by name with `-32601`,
// which is worth more than a broad surface that guesses: a skeleton
// answering one request correctly can be extended, and a server
// inventing answers has to be un-trusted first.
//
// DIAGNOSTICS ARE ALL THREE PHASES OR THEY ARE NOTHING. An editor
// showing type errors and silently not showing syntax errors teaches
// the user to distrust it, so lex's and parse's — which live on the
// `Build` — go out beside sema's, which live on the `Checker`.
//
// WHAT IS NOT BUILT, precisely, so nobody has to discover it:
//
//   - documentSymbol, definition, semanticTokens, references,
//     completion, formatting, signatureHelp, rename — L2 to L4.

WirePos*, LineRun*, Step*, to_pos*, to_wire*, run_of*, step_at* = lsp.lsp_pos
write_wire*, write_range* = lsp.lsp_pos
JsonId*, Run*, Pair*, Json*, Jsons*, write_text*, whole_of* = lsp.lsp_json
JsonFault*, Reader*, read*, push_utf8*, byte_of* = lsp.lsp_json_read
Envelope*, FrameFault*, frame_at*, write_frame*, write_decimal* = lsp.lsp_frame
short_by* = lsp.lsp_frame
Tell*, TypeAt*, ValueAt*, told_at*, is_nothing* = lsp.lsp_decl
Hover*, hover_at*, hover_in*, no_type* = lsp.lsp_hover
FILE_SCHEME*, path_of*, uri_at* = lsp.lsp_uri
Spot*, Diagnostics*, found_in*, publish*, ERROR* = lsp.lsp_diag
Server*, serve*, CAPABILITIES* = lsp.lsp_serve
frame_byte*, frame_why* = lsp.lsp_serve
Drain*, serve_stdio* = lsp.lsp_stdio
